  "body": "## What changed\n\nFoundational enabler for porting upstream's newer providers. Our `OpenAIChatProvider` and profile machinery are a **strict subset** of upstream's; ~18 of their providers need model-listing and reasoning-detail primitives we lack. This is **additive** and changes no user-visible behavior (PATCH).\n\nAdds, byte-for-byte from upstream (namespace-rewritten `free_claude_code` → `my_claude_code`):\n\n- `core/anthropic/openai_tool_names.py` — `OpenAIToolNameCodec` (reversible OpenAI tool aliases)\n- `core/anthropic/tool_schema.py` — JSON-schema helpers for text-emitted tool input\n- `core/anthropic/tools.py` — `FunctionTagToolParser` + function-tag constants\n- `core/anthropic/conversion.py` — `_SyntheticOpenAIToolTurnBoundary` + `is_synthetic_openai_tool_turn_boundary` + `_close_openai_tool_result_turns` (**defined but NOT wired into `convert_messages`** — that behavior change belongs to a later provider PR with its own test updates)\n- `core/anthropic/__init__.py` — re-export the three new names\n- `providers/model_listing.py` — `extract_openai_model_infos`, `extract_tool_capable_model_infos`, `model_list_items`, `validate_model_list_page`, `merge_model_list_pages`, `_path`/`_has_field`/`_MISSING`\n- `providers/openai_chat/reasoning_details.py` — structured reasoning replay + stream conversion\n- `providers/openai_chat/request_policy.py` — `_encode_openai_tool_names` + codec wiring\n- `providers/openai_chat/provider.py` — `OpenAIAsyncCredentialProvider` + `api_key_provider` support + `OpenAIModelListing`-driven `list_model_infos`/`_fetch_paginated_models_payload`\n- `providers/openai_chat/profiles.py` — `OpenAIModelPagination` + `OpenAIModelListing` dataclasses + two `OpenAIChatProfile` fields\n\n**Kept our fork's divergences intact** (OpenRouter vision detection via `_openrouter_accepts_images`, `supports_vision` field, `extract_openai_model_ids` returning `frozenset[str]`).\n\n## Verification\n\n- Full suite: **3861 passed / 6 failed** — the 6 are the documented pre-existing PowerShell-installer checksum failures, identical to unmodified `main`.\n- `ruff format --check`, `ruff check`, `ty check`: all clean.\n- A first attempt that *wired* `_close_openai_tool_result_turns` into `convert_messages` broke two `test_converter.py` tests (message-ordering behavior change) — reverted; wiring is deferred to the provider PR that owns that behavior.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- `_close_openai_tool_result_turns` is defined but not yet called — dead code until the `zenmux`/`cline_pass` PR wires it. Intentional: removing it while keeping `is_synthetic_openai_tool_turn_boundary` (used by `reasoning_details.py`) would leave a dangling helper.\n- This PR changes no provider behavior; the new machinery is only *consumed* once subsequent PRs add the providers.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
