    "message": "refactor(providers): port OpenAI model-listing + tool-name + reasoning-detail machinery\n\nFoundational enabler for porting upstream's newer providers. Our OpenAIChatProvider\nand profile machinery are a strict subset of upstream's; ~18 of their providers need\nmodel-listing and reasoning-detail primitives we lack. This is additive and changes no\nuser-visible behavior (PATCH).\n\nAdds (byte-for-byte from upstream, namespace-rewritten free_claude_code -> my_claude_code):\n- core/anthropic/openai_tool_names.py — OpenAIToolNameCodec (reversible OpenAI tool aliases)\n- core/anthropic/tool_schema.py — JSON-schema helpers for text-emitted tool input\n- core/anthropic/tools.py — FunctionTagToolParser + function-tag constants\n- core/anthropic/conversion.py — _SyntheticOpenAIToolTurnBoundary + is_synthetic_openai_tool_turn_boundary + _close_openai_tool_result_turns (defined; NOT wired into convert_messages yet — that behavior change lands in a later PR with its own test updates)\n- core/anthropic/__init__.py — re-export FunctionTagToolParser, OpenAIToolNameCodec, is_synthetic_openai_tool_turn_boundary\n- providers/model_listing.py — extract_openai_model_infos, extract_tool_capable_model_infos, model_list_items, validate_model_list_page, merge_model_list_pages, _path/_has_field/_MISSING\n- providers/openai_chat/reasoning_details.py — structured reasoning replay + stream conversion\n- providers/openai_chat/request_policy.py — _encode_openai_tool_names + codec wiring\n- providers/openai_chat/provider.py — OpenAIAsyncCredentialProvider + api_key_provider support + OpenAIModelListing-driven list_model_infos/_fetch_paginated_models_payload\n- providers/openai_chat/profiles.py — OpenAIModelPagination + OpenAIModelListing dataclasses + two OpenAIChatProfile fields\n\nKept our fork's own divergences intact (OpenRouter vision detection via _openrouter_accepts_images, supports_vision field, extract_openai_model_ids returning frozenset[str]).\n\nVerification: full suite 3861 passed / 6 pre-existing PS-installer failures (baseline unchanged); ruff format/check + ty clean. A first wiring attempt of _close_openai_tool_result_turns broke two test_converter tests (message-ordering behavior change) and was reverted — the wiring is intentionally deferred to the provider PR that owns that behavior.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
